  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Islam in a Secular State is a 2025 scholarly book by Walid Jumblatt Abdullah with an early and still limited impact record. The book has not yet accumulated citations in OpenAlex, but it does show initial signs of reach through library discovery and repository indexing.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The clearest signals for this book are structural rather than citation-based. It is indexed in repository infrastructure, appears in WorldCat holdings, and is connected to data citation workflows, which suggests that it is visible to library users, researchers, and scholarly metadata systems soon after publication.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">At the same time, the citation record is still empty in OpenAlex, so there is not yet evidence of downstream scholarly uptake in that source. The available record is therefore best read as an early-stage profile: the book is discoverable, but its longer-term academic influence has yet to emerge in citation data.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The broader attention record is also sparse. No event coverage is available in the archive used here, and the digest does not surface social or public-discourse signals that would indicate wider conversation. That absence should be interpreted cautiously, however, because some channels are simply not well captured for newer books.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the book\u2019s impact profile is modest but real: it is present in library and repository systems and has established metadata visibility, while the evidence for scholarly or public uptake remains limited at this stage.</p>",
